  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention: Global Malaria Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Through the U.S. President&apos;s Malaria Initiative (PMI), U.S. Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) provides scientific leadership in the public health efforts to fight malaria, increasing global understanding and capacity to prevent death and illness from malaria, especially among vulnerable populations. CDC science has made critical contributions to our understanding of the impact of drug resistance and ways to prevent its spread. In addition, CDC has long worked closely with National Malaria Control Programs to build their technical leadership and capacity to implement effective prevention and control. Through PMI, CDC continues this work, by sharing its technical expertise, particularly in the following areas: (1) design and implementation of monitoring and evaluation; (2) surveillance of malaria; (3) operational research; (4) case management (including diagnostics); (5) entomology/vector control; (6) laboratory support.</narrative>
  </description>
